5. THE LM5176'S OTHER SETTINGS AND R11 (the maker's equations)
   average current limit: ICL(AVG) = 50 mV / RSNS (Eq. 4, p.17): the ONE setting R11 sets; bands in section 3
   the CC loop: its gm amplifier (1 mS, p.7) discharges SS (C7 4.7u) when VSNS passes 50 mV (7.3.6, p.17): the loop's gain
     per ampere scales with R11, so the proposed loop acts at 0.62 of the held loop's gain (INFERRED); its response is a bench item
   the ISNS filter: 100 Ohm is the maker's ceiling (p.24) and R160, R161 are at it; unchanged. The bias offset is 0.3 mV either
     way, 48 mA at the proposed R11 against 30 mA at the held (in section 3's band)
   the current-sense amplifier's range: ISNS common mode 0 to 55 V (p.5) against VBUS20 at most 23.40 V (s120's bound): unchanged;
     ISNS(+) to ISNS(-) is rated +-0.3 V (p.5): at the proposed R11 that is 48 A, far past any current the path can carry
   slope compensation: Eq. 26 (p.24) uses RSENSE, the CS resistor R12, and L1, not R11: CSLOPE = gmSLOPE x L1 / (RSENSE x ACS)
     = 800 pF with 2 uS, 10 uH, 5 mOhm and 5 (the p.24 example's gm and gain), against C147 680p: unchanged by R11. If L1 runs
     near its Isat (section 4) its inductance falls and the dead-beat value falls with it (INFERRED)
   the cycle-by-cycle limits: boost peak 20 / 24 / 28 A and buck valley 13.2 / 16.0 / 18.8 A (VCS over R12 5 mOhm, p.7):
     unchanged; with the average limit raised they, not the average loop, bound L1 at a low VIN_RAW in an overload
   hiccup: MODE to VCC selects no hiccup (p.20), so a sustained overload stays in the average or the cycle-by-cycle limit
     indefinitely: at the proposed R11 it does so at the higher currents of section 4 (the held circuit sat there in service)

END. Desk figures on the makers' pages and the committed netlists; nothing is measured, nothing implemented.
